    "body": "## Summary\n\nAdds **ADR-050: @supports Conditional Rules**. **Documentation only.** Implementation (3 commits, ~350 lines) lands in a follow-up PR.\n\n**Closes a gap that has existed since CSS parsing was first vendored.** Every `@supports` block is currently dropped — 73 blocks in Wikipedia CSS, all lost.\n\n## Measurement (2026-10-29)\n\n### @supports blocks in Wikipedia CSS\n\n| Condition form | Count |\n|---|---|\n| `(A) or (B)` | 42 |\n| `not (...)` | 26 |\n| `(single feature)` | 5 |\n| **Total** | **73** |\n\n**22 of 73 nested inside `@media`** — the current parser explicitly skips nested at-rules, so those blocks are dropped twice.\n\n### Empirical test\n\n| Input | Rules parsed |\n|---|---|\n| `@supports (display: grid) { .x { color: red } }` | **0** |\n| `@supports not (display: grid) { .x { color: red } }` | **0** |\n| `@media (...) { @supports (...) { .x { color: red } } }` | **0** |\n| `.x { color: red }` (baseline) | **1** |\n\nEvery rule inside every `@supports` block is currently lost.\n\n### Unique conditions (all 10)\n\n```\n(display: grid)\n(width: round(1.5px, 1px))\n(text-decoration: underline dotted)\n(word-break: break-word)\n(overflow-wrap: anywhere)\n(-webkit-mask-image: none) or (mask-image: none)\nnot ((-webkit-mask-image: none) or (mask-image: none))\nnot selector(:focus-visible)\n```\n\n## The critical design subtlety\n\n**Unconditional include would double-render icons.**\n\nWikipedia pairs two blocks:\n```css\n@supports not (mask-image) { .icon { background-image: url(x.svg); } }\n@supports (mask-image)     { .icon { mask-image: url(x.svg); background-color: #202122; } }\n```\n\nBoth properties are **additive, not competing** — our paint order draws bg-image over mask (per ADR-034 + ADR-047). Both in cascade → **double-rendered icons**.\n\n**Solution**: feature-query evaluation against a hardcoded capability table. Capability table marks `mask-image` as supported → the `not (mask-image)` block evaluates `false` → correctly excluded.\n\n## Scope\n\n### Commit 1 — Parse + capability table + evaluator\n- `feature_query_supported(prelude)` with supported properties, values, pseudos\n- Unsupported-value checks: `round`, `sqrt`, `sin`, `cos`, `tan`, `dotted`, `dashed`\n- Top-level `@supports` branch in `parse()`\n- `@media`-nested `@supports`: recursive parse (replaces `skip_at_rule`)\n- Behavior-neutral for all existing tests (none use `@supports`)\n\n### Commit 2 — Tests + visual verification\n- 15 unit tests in `test_stylesheet.cpp`\n- Layout test: `.vector-pinned-container` gets `display: block` (was `none`)\n- First-viewport PNG: sidebar TOC renders (or documented zero-delta if other culling rules block it)\n- ADR-047 icon regression check (double-render must NOT happen)\n\n### Commit 3 — Docs\n- ADR-050 → Implemented\n- Post-ADR-050 note in ADR-027\n- README + CHANGELOG\n\n## Deferred\n\n- Runtime feature detection (probe-based)\n- `@supports` with complex `selector(...)` args\n- Nested `@supports` inside `@supports` (0 uses)\n- `@supports font-tech(...)` / `font-format(...)` (not in target)\n- Capability table auto-derivation\n\n## Reviewer checklist\n\n- [ ] **Feature-query evaluation (not unconditional include)** — required for `@supports not (mask-image)` correctness. Would otherwise double-render every icon. Agree?\n- [ ] **Parse-time gate** — `@supports` is static feature detection, no per-element variance. Unlike `@media` which must be cascade-time. Agree?\n- [ ] **Hardcoded capability table** — 10 unique conditions in target; runtime probing is ~200 extra lines. Acceptable v1 scope?\n- [ ] **`@media`-nested `@supports`** — 22 of 73 blocks; must work in v1 or we drop 30% of blocks.\n- [ ] **Mask-image capability entry** — necessary for correct `not (mask-image)` exclusion. Verified against ADR-047's existing mask rules.\n\n## Test plan\n\nNo code touched. Post-merge: `cmake --build build && ./build/tests/honeybee_tests` — 611 / 2386 unchanged.\n\n## ADR\n\n`docs/decisions/050-supports.md` — status Accepted; implementation in follow-up PR.\n\nRefs #230\n",
